flowchart TB
accTitle: Reading a cast from your own node
accDescr: The browser asks for casts over HTTPS. On the server, the client service reads the node database and sends the posts back. The repeated service and browser boxes show the return trip, not extra software.
browser["Farcaster client in your browser"]:::device
subgraph S["Your AWS server"]
 client["Client service"]:::service
 node[("Snapchain database")]:::data
 result["Same client service"]:::service
end
feed["Your browser shows the feed"]:::done
browser -->|"1 · Ask for casts · HTTPS"| client
client -->|"2 · Read stored casts"| node
node -->|"3 · Return the posts"| result
result -->|"4 · Feed over HTTPS"| feed
style S fill:#f5faf8,stroke:#aac7be
classDef device fill:#f1edff,stroke:#795acb,color:#24183e,stroke-width:1.5px
classDef service fill:#ffffff,stroke:#8b819d,color:#262330,stroke-width:1.4px
classDef data fill:#eaf6f2,stroke:#3c7b68,color:#173c31,stroke-width:1.5px
classDef network fill:#fff5e5,stroke:#997033,color:#493414,stroke-width:1.5px
classDef done fill:#eaf6f2,stroke:#3c7b68,color:#173c31,stroke-width:1.5px
